From 9d645f33036923d337b16d05afb940011258aca9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Collado <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:08:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Pad: libpad2 (scePad2*) and libdbc (sceDbc*) served by the
 libpad host input

Games built with later SCE SDKs read the controller through libpad2 sockets
(scePad2CreateSocket/GetState/Read/GetButtonProfile) on top of libdbc, not
libpad. PS2Recomp only served libpad, so such a game saw no controller: its
socket never connected and every "press a button" screen waited forever
(Outbreak, SLPM-65428, stops at its first memory-card prompt).

Each socket maps onto a libpad port opened in DualShock 2 mode with pressures,
so the keyboard/gamepad backend, the test override and the debug snapshot are
shared. scePad2Read returns libpad's data from byte 2 on (buttons active-low in
the SCE big-endian order, sticks, 12 pressures), length 18; the button profile
reports every button, so a game treats the pad as a DualShock 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
